     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Noto Serif&#39;,serif;font-size:19px;line-height:31.9997997283936px\">One of the things I really like about shiny</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Noto Serif&#39;,serif;font-size:19px;line-height:31.9997997283936px\"> is that it has excellent documentation: the tutorial, the articles and the gallery go a long way in helping newcomers as well as intermediate programmers mastering the structure and features of shiny. Still, there are a few things I found lacking from the documentation but important to understand especially if your shiny app is going to be more than just a few lines of R code. I’m sharing them here hoping they can help others avoid some of the roundabouts I took as I learn my way in shiny (follow the link to my blog post to get the detail on each topic below):</span><br><div><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&#39;Noto Serif&#39;,serif;font-size:19px;line-height:31.9997997283936px\"><br></span></div><div><ul style=\"box-sizing:inherit;border:0px;font-family:&#39;Noto Serif&#39;,serif;font-size:19px;margin:0px 0px 1.6842em;outline:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline;color:rgb(51,51,51);line-height:31.9997997283936px\"><li style=\"box-sizing:inherit;border:0px;font-family:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-weight:inherit;margin:0px;outline:0px;padding:0px;vertical-align:baseline\"><a href=\"https://shinydata.wordpress.com/2015/02/02/a-few-things-i-learned-about-shiny-and-reactive-programming/#reactive-dependencies-are-dynamic\" style=\"box-sizing:inherit;font-family:inherit;font-style:inherit;font-weight:inherit;outline:0px;color:rgba(51,51,51,0.701961)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://shinydata.wordpress.com/2015/02/02/a-few-things-i-learned-about-shiny-and-reactive-programming/%23reactive-dependencies-are-dynamic&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792400465386000&amp;usg=AOvVaw